:: "Maybe we would've handled it better if you helped." {"position":"2000,450","size":"100,100"}
	Dawn glares at you, "Maybe I would've helped if you remembered that there's a clearing that way, where Dusk was leading the guards so I could pick them off for you. You're the one who decided to take that fight early, in the middle of the woods!"
    Your injured arm throbs in pain with your rise in indignation. You're about to snap back when Dusk gets between you, trying to placate you both with a smile.
    He speaks in a calm voice, "Hey, we won the fight. No fight goes perfectly, and we all did what we thought was best. Remember: Kin'eer and Alkin have their fight, which we should go help with. We're a team, we can figure out a fight, right? We've done it a hundred times before."
    You don't feel like letting this go just yet, but at least Dusk is right about one thing: Kin'eer and Alkin need your help. Dawn appears to agree, and you all start heading back to the tower. Dawn walks slightly apart from and in front of everyone else, obviously upset. Vylin sighs and walks to the front of the group to talk with her. You can't hear what they're talking about but you see Dawn snap at Vylin, which makes Vylin flinch. This just makes you angrier at Dawn, but then you see Vylin compose himself and he starts talking calmly back to Dawn. Courageous, but Dawn isn't easy to appease.... But she doesn't snap back, instead she starts talking at a reasonable volume, which makes Vylin visibly relax. Dusk hangs back to talk with you.
    "So, why'd you turn around? Just forgot about the clearing?"
|1>[(link: "-\"No...\" (Lie)")[
He still smiles, even though he instantly sees through your lie.
	He calmly explains, "I know you forgot. I didn't remember until we had already been running for a while, and even then I'm pretty sure I was lost. I would have found my way eventually, but my point is that you shouldn't feel bad about Dawn getting like that. She just-.... She doesn't like it when she feels like she's being asked to do something she doesn't want to do, and she sure didn't want to fight all the guards."
    (hide: ?2)
|3>[(Link: "-\"Well I didn't want to either, but I did!\"")[
	Dusk sighs, "You aren't Dawn. If you knew her like I did, you'd give her more slack. I try not to excuse her actions too much, but I think you're being a little harsh on her."
    Dawn turns around, her fox ears twitching, "If you two are done talking about me, we're at the tower."
    Sure enough, in front of you is the tower that Kin'eer and Alkin stayed at, and they're already cleaning up the bodies of the guards they fought.
    Alkin looks up, smiling and waving, "Looks like you all dealt with your fight well enough! Oh, but you...."
    Alkin and Kin'eer notice how you're hurt, but at this point you just shrug. But then Dusk motions for you to sit down, and he starts to heal you. As he does so you also notice that Alkin himself is hurt.
-(Link-goto: "Let Dusk heal you")[
]
-(Link-goto: "Ask Dusk to heal Alkin")[
]
(Set: $Duskfriend to $Duskfriend-5)
(hide: ?4)
]]
|4>[(Link: "-\"I guess I understand. I just wish she'd be less extreme. Do you know what I mean?\"")[
	Dusk smiles and nods, "Oh, yeah, I do. Then again, she has her reasons. Just give her some time, okay? It took her years to warm up to me, and we grew up together."
        Dawn turns around, her fox ears twitching, "If you two are done talking about me, we're at the tower."
    Sure enough, in front of you is the tower that Kin'eer and Alkin stayed at, and they're already cleaning up the bodies of the guards they fought.
    Alkin looks up, smiling and waving, "Looks like you all dealt with your fight well enough! Oh, but you...."
    Alkin and Kin'eer notice how you're hurt, but at this point you just shrug. Dusk then motions for you to sit down, and he starts to heal you. As he does so you also notice that Alkin himself is hurt.
-(Link-goto: "Let Dusk heal you")[
]
-(Link-goto: "Ask Dusk to heal Alkin")[
]
