:: "This is a wizard tower. It might be that the delay is long enough for a wizard to counter-spell it." [Potion-get] {"position":"225,675","size":"100,100"}
	Dusk nods, "My thoughts exactly. Now, I just need to think of a counter-spell. It's hard, since I can't think of any way to figure out what the trap is, other than the fact it's magical."
    Kin'eer presents an idea, "What if the wizard wasn't the catalyst for the counter-spell? Perhaps a button, enchanted item, or potion would be used?"
    Dusk thinks for a moment before speaking, "Maybe, but that just means we'd have to find it. The mercenaries were looting the place, so I guess you're thinking that they may have found this enchanted item?"
    Kin'eer nods, and before anyone goes off looking, you present the potion.
    Dusk examines it, and then shrugs, "This could be it, but I have no clue what the potion actually does. There's still a bunch of magical noise messing with my sight right now, so all I can say is that it's not the strongest potion. Maybe it'd protect you from the trap, but it's hard to say."
    Alkin then walks up and takes the potion himself, "One way to find out."
    He starts walking to the door, preparing to uncork the potion, but Kin'eer stops him.
    She keeps her voice even when she chastises, "Idiot. You leap before you look, like most dwarfs. I have armor, so if there's any trap that the potion doesn't protect against, or if there's enemies in the next room, I should be the one that tests the door."
    Then Vylin walks up, entering the conversation, "Actually, it should be me. I found the lever to delay the trap, and I'm the least useful member. If I get hurt I can just stay back."
    Dusk shakes his head, "No. I wouldn't leave you injured so I'd stay back and heal you, and they need the both of us. I should do it. I know the most magic out of all of us, and so if something goes wrong then maybe I can counter-spell the trap. This is my specialty, so let me do it."
    You notice that Dawn doesn't offer.
-[[Let Alkin go]]
-[[Let Kin'eer go]]
-[[Let Vylin go]]
-[[Let Dusk go]]
-[[Make Dawn go]]
-[[Go yourself]]
--(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: "To fool people into opening it, thinking they disarmed the trapped door when they really didn't?" [Potion-get] {"position":"100,800","size":"100,100"}
	Kin'eer nods, "That's what I would do. I bet that there's another secret entrance into the next room."
    Vylin sighs, "So what you're saying is that we need to keep searching the room?"
    Everyone pauses expectantly. That would seem to be the case.
    But before everyone splits, Dusk gets everyone's attention again, "Wait. The mercenaries looted the room before we did. You think they found anything useful? Has anyone looted them yet?"
    You step forward, showing the potion. Dusk grabs it from you, using his magic sight to try and figure out what the potion does....
    He shrugs, "Yeah, I've got nothing. It has some faint magical traces, but I'm not sure if it'd protect you from a trap, or deactivate the trap in any way."
    Alkin then walks up and takes the potion himself, "One way to find out."
    He starts walking to the door, preparing to uncork the potion, but Kin'eer stops him.
    She keeps her voice even when she chastises, "Idiot. You leap before you look, like most dwarfs. I have armor, so if there's any trap that the potion doesn't protect against, or if there's enemies in the next room, I should be the one that tests the door."
    Then Vylin walks up, entering the conversation, "Actually, it should be me. I found the lever to delay the trap, and I'm the least useful member. If I get hurt I can just stay back."
    Dusk shakes his head, "No. I wouldn't leave you injured so I'd stay back and heal you, and they need the both of us. I should do it. I know the most magic out of all of us, and so if something goes wrong then maybe I can counter-spell the trap. This is my specialty, so let me do it."
    You notice that Dawn doesn't offer.
-[[Let Alkin go]]
-[[Let Kin'eer go]]
-[[Let Vylin go]]
-[[Let Dusk go]]
-[[Make Dawn go]]
-[[Go yourself]]
--(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


