:: Agree with Dawn {"position":"650,875","size":"100,100"}



:: Are you really going? [You-hurt] {"position":"1425,375","size":"100,100"}
	Kin'eer and Alkin look at each other. Alkin shrugs and Kin'eer sighs a deep, exasperated sigh.
    "Fine. But please for the love of Wisdom don't die."
    She helps you to your feet, and though you're still wobbly you have a strange feeling that you need to get away from this tower for a moment.
    The walk in the woods is easy, though, and Dawn, Dusk, and Vylin are easy enough to find. They even seem to have handled most of the guards themselves. There's still a few guards but Kin'eer and Alkin are already rushing forward to help. None of them seem injured so you could probably just stay back... Then again, you could go and help in the already ending fight, even though you're injured. What's the worst that happens?
-[[Help in the fight]]
-[[Stay back]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Ask Dusk to heal Alkin {"position":"2050,550","size":"100,100"}



:: Check out the sound {"position":"1825,575","size":"100,100"}



:: Check the room [Vylin-injured] {"position":"750,150","size":"100,100"}
	Right, first you should check the rest of the room. What if there had been enemies in there and you had started a fight while Dusk was in the middle of healing Vylin? Or what if the door was trapped?! You didn't even think about that until you stopped to think about it for a second. Thank goodness you didn't let your curiosity get the better of you.
    First, you look around the room for anything important, and your eyes fall on the bookshelf that the mercenaries on the left were investigating. You look about at the point they were looking at, and find books strewn about like they were looking for something. Then your eyes fall on a book that's not dusty, but looks like it hasn't been moved. Curious, you pull the book off the shelf, but it only comes off halfway before stopping, which is when you hear a click coming from the door.
    Everyone in the party, except for Dusk and Vylin, looks up at you and the door. Dawn walks over, checking the book you just pulled from the shelf.
    She nods, "Good find. Door was probably trapped."
    Alkin also walks over, nodding. He then starts to walk to the door to open it when Kin'eer stops him.
    She says, "Wait. There could be another trap, and we can't afford any new messes with Vylin and Dusk busy. Let Dawn check it. She did well with the last door, she'll probably do fine with this one."
    Dawn accepts the compliment without a word, and she starts sniffing the door. She can smell magic, for some reason. It's kind of like the magical sight that Dusk has. She waits a little longer before stepping away from the door.
    Dawn explains, "Yeah, the door's still trapped. The book made it so that the trap would be delayed enough for a quick mage to cast a counterspell, but it still would have went off. We should disarm it."
    Alkin, though a little pale at the realization that he was about to activate the trap if Kin'eer didn't stop him, still puts in his two cents, "Surely we don't need to do that again? Can't we just find a way around the trap? What if there's a secret entrance? Or what if there's a simpler way to disarm the trap?"
    Dawn and Kin'eer pause, looking at each other. Neither say anything, and then all three look at you. Well, time to do your job.
-[[Disarm trap]]
-[[Look for another way]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


