:: Continue [You-hurt] {"position":"1450,625","size":"100,100"}
	As Dusk heals you as gently as he can, Kin'eer walks over to look at you. It's a mix of disappointment and gratefulness.
    She speaks softer than she usually does, "You're worse off than before. You should have stayed... but Dusk is right, at least you're getting healed. I won't question your choice."
    That sentence right there might as well have been a deep bow of respect from her, but you're trying too hard not to flinch as Dusk heals you to really appreciate it. Kin'eer doesn't seem to mind as she goes to help clean up after the fight.


:: Continue down the secret passage {"position":"1100,700","size":"100,100"}



:: Disarm trap [Vylin-injured Dawn-injured] {"position":"750,450","size":"100,100"}
	You motion for Dawn to give it her best shot, and she kneels in front of the door with her picking tools out. Everyone else backs up far enough away that if the trap gets set off only Dawn will be in the radius.... You're checking on Dusk and Vylin when suddenly-
    
    ***BOOM!!!***
    
    Dusk looks up from Vylin, towards the explosion that came from where Dawn was working on the door, and he points at you while he's still bandaging Vylin. It's an obvious command to go check on Dawn, but he didn't need to ask you twice. The party quickly goes into the next room, trying to put out enough fires along the way to not catch fire themselves. What kind of explosion could set stuff even way back in the first hallway on fire? Eventually you fight enough fire to make it to the room with the mercenaries, and in the center of the inferno you see Dawn putting out fires around her. With Kin'eer's rudimentary magical skills she manages to help Dawn, and you run up to make sure she's okay.
    Dawn assures, "I'm fine, yes. It's just fire. I've been resistant to fire since I was a child. Like Alkin, in a way."
    You see how she favors her left leg, and you can see the soot all across her clothes. She'll probably survive, but she's not in the best shape.
-[[Make her go to Dusk for healing]]
-[[Accept her assurance]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Don't??? [Potion-get] {"position":"250,1075","size":"100,100"}
	.... TO HELL WITH THIS! You throw open the door, because who needs a potion?! Someone who's probably going to get their head removed by a trap they don't actually have any information on?! NEVER! You throw the door open.
    
    ***BOOM***
    
    .... Well, ow. Like, very much ow. That was not a good idea, seeing as how the door blew up and sent you flying across the room in a fireball. You're lying on the ground, on fire, and in pain. Before you know it, Dusk is standing above you using magic to put the fire out and heal you.
    "Hey, hey, stay with me. Don't pass out, you'll be so much harder to heal then."
    You feel some of the burn wounds cool down and heat up at the same time, which you know is what all of Dusk's healing feels like. Your head feels really, really fuzzy. Like there's a campfire in your head, your thoughts flicker. Your head spins. Wow, this was a really bad idea. Who thought it'd be a good idea to open the trapped door without a potentially life-saving potion? That person should be fired (heh, fired) from making decisions ever again.
    Slowly, as you come around to steady consciousness, you see the rest of the party looking down at you like you're crazy.
    Vylin is pacing in the back, talking to himself, "Oh my god, did the potion not work? Or was the explosion too powerful? Or maybe we needed to use the potion and a counter-spell at the same-"
    Kin'eer kneels next to you, taking the potion from your bag, and then she interrupts, "No, I think our plan would have worked. It's the fact that they never drank the potion."
    Everyone stares at you as you slowly sit up, your mind and body finally working. Dusk looks absolutely worn out as he sits on the floor next to you.
    He groans, "Well, I'm out of mana. Was it worth it?"
-[[Explain how you aren't an idiot->Idiot]]
-[[Accept you made the wrong choice->Idiot]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Drink the potion {"position":"350,850","size":"100,100"}
(set:$Items to $Items - (a: "Potion"))
    You uncork the bottle and drink the potion, quickly just in case it doesn't last that long. It tastes like... water, really. Maybe slightly of iron? You don't focus too much on that, and instead just open the door when you finish the potion, throwing the bottle to the side.
    
    ***BOOM!!!***
    
    OW! The door explodes and you get flung back across the room. Before you know it, Dusk is already standing over you, checking for wounds, but... you feel fine. The rest of the party enters the room as you sit up, checking yourself for injuries. You have none, and the second Dusk realises that, he starts putting out fires around the room with his magic.
    WOOO! You throw your hands up. That was a rush of... so many emotions, but you're alive! On shaking legs, you slowly stand, Alkin helping you stay steady. He also looks you up and down, but when he also sees no injuries, he slaps you on the back with a laugh.
    He tries to sound like he wasn't terrified, "I knew your courage would keep you up, trap or no! A little explosion couldn't keep down the likes of you!"
    Dusk then turns and explains, "I think I see. The potion wasn't quite a fire resistance potion, but it gave you the temporary ability to not change in temperature. A simple spell that's useful for keeping a room to a desired temperature, but I've never thought about using it on a person. Clever."
    You nod, having to agree. Anything that keeps you alive from an explosion is very clever indeed.
    Kin'eer then steps forward, "Well then, the next room needs to be cleared. Let us hope that one trap and a group of mercenaries was enough for this wizard."
    Dusk and Alkin both look at each other, containing a laugh. With this party's luck you might only have to fight fifty more mercenaries while you disarm ten more traps, and maybe stop a cult or two.
    -[[Continue->Room 2]]


:: Fall back and try to get Kin'eer and Alkin's help [You-hurt] {"position":"1625,250","size":"100,100"}
	You're hurt and outclassed, plus Alkin and Kin'eer are your martial specialists, so you definitely need their help. You start falling back, just doing the bare minimum with your injured arm to keep yourself safe. You feel your back press up into Kin'eer's broad shoulderblades, and she seems to instantly recognize you need help. In a swift motion she steps back, spinning around you so that you can take her enemy and she can take all of yours. You follow her motion, and come face-to-face with two injured guards. Not an easy fight, but better than fighting three healthy ones. You and the guards fight sparingly, not committing to any large attacks or trying to push, for you both seem fairly even in skill. It's obvious that you're both hoping your allies will save you, but you know your allies well enough to know that they aren't losing this fight.
    Right as you think that, you see Alkin join your side, his enemies lying on the floor with bashed armor. You both push and defeat your enemies, again turning to help Kin'eer but finding her enemies similarly felled.
    You sit down, sighing and immediately checking your wound. It could be worse, but it's also far from good. Kin'eer is already kneeling by your side while Alkin checks the bodies.
    She gently grabs your wrist, turning it as she talks about it, "I think you should be fine once Dusk comes back. He has all of our healing supplies but ran off with Dawn and Vylin. I doubt the guards that chased them won any significant hits, but fighting in a forest is a battle of attrition. Their fight might not be over, so I'm going to find them."
    Alkin then pipes up, gesturing at you, "And we're just going to leave them here, injured?"
    Kin'eer nods, "We won't be long, and all the guards are dealt with. They're a grown adult, they can handle themselves, even injured. Unless you think they should come and fight with us?"
-[[Go with them]]
-[[Stay]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Follow Dawn and Vylin {"position":"250,400","size":"100,100"}
	You follow Dawn and Vylin, approaching the five mercenaries looting the bookshelf. Dawn has her bow in her hand and Vylin is holding a dagger. Suddenly, from behind you there's a clash of metal. The fight has started, and Dawn puts an arrow into the chest of one of the five mercenaries in front of you. It doesn't drop him, but it slows him down enough to turn this into a four versus three. You draw your sword and start fighting one of the guards while Vylin strums his lyre to put a firebolt into another. You each defeat your enemy, and then turn on the last standing one together. You win your fight without injury as Vylin ties up the injured mercenary that Dawn shot, who apparently stayed down after getting hit. You turn to help Dusk, Kin'eer, and Alkin with their fight but they're already done at the same time you are. Kin'eer is already moving the bodies respectfully to the corner. Hopefully you can at least give them a pyre when you leave. Dawn has started checking for traps, Dusk is walking over to heal the mercenary that got shot, and Alkin is checking the area that the mercenaries were arguing in to see if they left any clues as to why they were hired. After Vylin ties up the mercenary and lets Dusk take over, he joins Dawn in checking for traps, though he starts by the bookcase that the mercenaries were inspecting.
    You take a quick glance around while your party deals with the aftermath of the fight, and you see the door to the next room. It's not locked as far as you can tell, so you could probably go ahead and open it.
-[[Open the next door]]
-[[Help your party clear the room]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Follow Dusk, Kin'eer, and Alkin [Vylin-injured] {"position":"600,75","size":"100,100"}
(set: $Vylinhealth to 10)
    You go right towards the less distracted of the guards, assuming this is where the fight will be the toughest, since this is where it'll start. Turns out it doesn't take long for you to be proven right. Right before you get close enough to strike, one of the guards notices you and yells. The fight starts, and with Dusk, Kin'eer, and Alkin by your side, even a dozen mercenaries are fodder, just as they predicted. You've all been adventuring so long that you should've known that this would be easy. You barely manage to strike a single mercenary once before they're all crumpled on the ground.
    You then turn to Dawn and Vylin, expecting them to have had a similarly easy time, but it seems like something unexpected happened. Dawn is outnumbered, three to one, and Vylin is bleeding badly on the floor. Dusk joins the fight first, followed by Kin'eer, then you, then Alkin. You take one of the mercenaries yourself, but even as the fight easily ends it's too late to keep Vylin safe. Dusk is down next to him ready to heal right as the last mercenary drops, and you step back, knowing that you'll only make things more complicated by interfering with Dusk's work.
    Instead, you look around the room, knowing that you need to secure the location before you do anything else. The first thing that caught your eye is the door across the room. It doesn't even look like it can lock. You think it might lead into the next room, and you should probably make sure it's clear of enemies.
-[[Open door]]
-[[Check the room]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Go back and make sure you really didn't miss anything [Extra-info Vylin-injured] {"position":"925,425","size":"100,100"}
(set: $Items to $Items + (a: "Book"))
    You go back into the room, searching for secret levers, buttons, chests, items, anything. You don't find anything immensely useful, and the rest of the party seems to be getting just a little impatient.
    Vylin pipes up, "Hey, we checked that room, like, seven times. I think it's clear."
    Okay, maybe more than a little impatient. Then again, you do find an interesting book on magical botany. Probably not useful, but you take it so you can read it at camp, maybe.
-[[Continue->Naw, time to keep going]] 


:: Go back and through the trapped door out of curiosity [Vylin-injured Potion-get Dusk-tired You-hurt] {"position":"925,825","size":"100,100"}
	You suddenly head back, motioning for everyone to get safely back from the door you're about to open. Before anyone can stop you, you throw the door wide open. How bad can the trap be, anyway?
    
    ***BOOM***
    
    .... Well, ow. Like, very much ow. That was not a good idea, seeing as how the door blew up and sent you flying across the room in a fireball. You're lying on the ground, on fire, and in pain. Before you know it, Dusk is standing above you using magic to put the fire out and heal you.
    "Hey, hey, stay with me. Don't pass out, you'll be so much harder to heal then."
    You feel some of the burn wounds cool down and heat up at the same time, which you know is what all of Dusk's healing feels like. Your head feels really, really fuzzy. Like there's a campfire in your head, your thoughts flicker. Your head spins. Wow, this was a really bad idea. That person should be fired (heh, fired) from making decisions ever again.
    Slowly, as you come around to steady consciousness, you see the rest of the party looking down at you like you're crazy.
    You try to sit up, but Dusk stops you, making you lay down again.
    "Don't even think about it. What came over you? You knew the door was trapped, right?"
    Kin'eer nods, "We all did. Dawn told us."
    Dusk sighs, "Well, whatever. We have a choice though. Are we going through the secret passageway or the trapped one?"
-[[Secret passage->You're silly]]
-[[Trapped door->You're silly]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Go check the next room {"position":"650,1025","size":"100,100"}



:: Go to the room past the trapped door {"position":"650,750","size":"100,100"}
	You hold your hand out to stop her, explaining that it might be a better idea to keep going to the room past the trapped door. Kin'eer raises her eyebrow, but considers it.
    Vylin actually nods, supporting you, "Wait, $Player has a point. That trap was pretty powerful, but most of us were pretty far back when it went off. Whatever lies past that door may expect us to be more hurt than we are. That's an advantage."
    The rest of the party pauses, but Kin'eer seems the most hesitant.
    "I am not confident in that idea. The enemy wants us to continue that way, but I doubt they expected us to find this alternative course of action. If we want to catch them off guard then this is the direction we should go."
    You then explain that what would actually be the most unexpected thing would be to do both. That gets Kin'eer's attention.
    Dusk, on the other hand, immediately speaks against it, "Whoa, wait. Split up? Do you want to get picked off by horrific creatures hiding in the walls? Because that's how you get picked off by horrific creatures hiding in the walls."
    Dawn shrugs, "I don't know, maybe they have a point. It's not like we're going on our own, and we can split the party in a way that keeps both sides with a mage, a martial, and a utility. Dusk, Vylin, and Alkin can go through the trapped door while the rest of us go through the new passage."
    Dusk pauses, but relents, "Fine. But only if everyone agrees."
    Everyone nods their head, all except for you.
-[[Agree with Dawn]]
-[[Swap with Vylin]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Go with them [You-hurt] {"position":"1550,375","size":"100,100"}
	You try to stand, shaking your head, but you instantly go lightheaded and sit back down.
    Kin'eer looks up as if in prayer, and says with exasperation, "Please, oh please tell me that wasn't you trying to come with us. Look, I trust your decisions most of the time, but *stay*."
    Alkin nods, agreeing, "I'm with Kin'eer. I'm sorry, but you're in no fighting condition. If it weren't for you, that last fight would've gone worse, and now you deserve rest. You took a hit for us, so don't make it in vain."
-[[Are you really going?]]
-[[Stay]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Go yourself [Potion-get] {"position":"200,900","size":"100,100"}
    You step forward, taking the potion for yourself. You motion for the others to go back, far enough away that they won't get hurt if something bad happens. You take a deep breath as they do what you tell them to.... It's time to do this, but your hands are shaking. What if the potion doesn't help? What if it's not trapped, and you actually have to use the potion later? What if, what if, what if.... It's time to actually do this, no matter how scared you might be.
    -[[Drink the potion]]
    -[[Don't???]]


:: Help in the fight {"position":"1275,400","size":"100,100"}



:: Help your party clear the room [Potion-get] {"position":"125,550","size":"100,100"}
(set:$Items to $Items + (a: "Potion"))
    Right, clear the room first. Kin'eer would chastise you for wandering off on your own if you went to the next room before this one was secure.
    You decide to check on the bodies in the corner, making sure they don't have anything important on them, like a key. You don't find anything quite like that, but you do find an interesting potion. You're not entirely sure on what it does, but you can probably just ask Dusk when he gets done healing the injured guard.
    Suddenly, you hear two clicks, one by the door you didn't open and one by the bookshelf that you fought by. Vylin is standing with a book halfway removed from the shelf. It's a hidden lever!
    Dawn walks up to Vylin, nodding, "Nice find. Probably disarmed the trap by the door."
    Dusk then stands, wiping the blood from his hands as he gathers everyone together to say, "I healed the guard, but he doesn't know anything important. We can figure out what to do with him when we get back from the top of the tower."
    Kin'eer raises her eyebrow, "Top of the tower? Isn't the mission to find the wizard?"
    Dusk nods, "Yeah, and where else would he be except the top of the tower?"
    Alkin pipes up, "Basement? It's safer underground than way high up, right?"
    Vylin stifles a laugh, "Sure you're not just saying that because you're scared of heights?"
    Alkin glares at Vylin, "Dwarfs aren't meant to be in the air! Ground or water, those are the places dwarfs belong!"
    Kin'eer looks from Dusk, to Alkin, to Vylin, then breaks up the argument, "This has gotten out of hand, and wasn't the intent for bringing us together, right Dusk?"
    Dusk nods, "Right. My point was that the next door is trapped."
    Vylin rolls his eyes, "Yeah, we figured that out when I pulled the lever in the bookshelf."
    Dusk shakes his head, "No, I mean that it's still trapped. When you pulled the lever some of the magic in the air dissipated, and I can see a bit clearer now. Pulling the lever made it so the trap on the door will be delayed, but not disarmed."
    Vylin tilts his head, asking, "Who makes a trap like that? What's the point of having a trap you can delay but not disarm?"
-[["To fool people into opening it, thinking they disarmed the trapped door when they really didn't?"]]
-[["This is a wizard tower. It might be that the delay is long enough for a wizard to counter-spell it."]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Idiot [Potion-get Dusk-tired You-hurt] {"position":"275,1200","size":"100,100"}
	Before you even have the chance to open your mouth, Kin'eer holds up a hand to silence you.
    "No. Don't talk. You need rest, and I'm not in the mood to explain to you how much of an idiot you are."
    She stands, and walks to the new hole in the wall.
    "We have a new room to clear. Dusk, Vylin, stay here with them while they recover. Dawn, Alkin, you're with me."
    She goes into the next room, and too tired to argue you just lay back down onto the ground, resting with Dusk while Vylin keeps guard.


:: Ignore the sound {"position":"1725,650","size":"100,100"}



:: Keep fighting by yourself {"position":"1475,175","size":"100,100"}
	Yes, you do have to keep fighting. Kin'eer and Alkin are both fighting their fights, and you're fighting yours. You start using your shield more, letting the enemies come closer so you can quickly jab with your injured arm without putting too much strain on it.
(if: (random: 1,20) <= 20)[
	But one of the times that you jab out, you hit one of the guards across their platemail, and you lose grip of your sword! You try to scramble for it behind your shield, but your arm is starting to feel weaker and a guard kicks the sword away. You try again, but a sword lashes out, striking your shoulder. You feel your arm go limp, and you start hiding behind your shield more completely, trying to take as many hits as you can before you get helped. Suddenly you see a blur as a mace goes into one of the guard's helmets. Kin'eer is at your side, and she takes on the guards, Alkin joining you moments later.
    They both, working together, win the fight easily, and you sit down the second the last guard drops, nursing your arm. Kin'eer and Alkin approach, and Kin'eer instantly starts checking your wounds.
    She tries to be gentle, but she's not very good at it, twisting your arm this way and that way, "Alkin, I think we need Dusk. $Player will be fine, I think, but-.... I'd feel more confident if he were here."
    Alkin nods, "Of course. You can stay here with $Player, I can go find Dusk and the others. Knowing them, they won their fight without a problem."
    Kin'eer nods and Alkin runs off into the woods. Kin'eer goes back to treating your wound, though there's not much else she can do. You're pretty sure she's just checking it over and over again to keep herself busy.
    (Set: $Youhealth to $Youhealth - 5)
|1>[(link: "-\"You know you don't have to do that, right? Like you said, I'll be fine.\"")[
	Kin'eer pauses, letting go of your arm and sighing, "Okay. You're right. I'll just stand guard instead."
    She stands, taking her weapon in her hand as she stands in front of you, checking over the dead guards and the nearby woods. She wanders a bit away, and you let out a sigh as you start to check your own wound. It hurts badly, and you feel your entire arm throbbing. It feels horrible, but you'll be fine, right? You think you start hearing things as a sharp scratching sound comes from behind you, deep in the tower. You hope it's just your mind playing tricks on you, but you doubt it.
   |2>[ (link: "-Check on the sound yourself")[
    (go-to: "Check out the sound")
    (set: $Kinfriend to $Kinfriend - 5)
    ]]
    (link: "-Wait for Kin'eer")[
    You wait for Kin'eer to do her rounds, and when she comes closer you get her attention, and point behind you, explaining what you heard. She nods without question, and moves to go check it out.
    |3>[(link: "-\"I trust you, but still be careful.\"")[
    (Set: $Kinfriend to $Kinfriend +5)
    She pauses, looks back, and nods again. She appears slightly confused as she continues, but you think you see the hint of a smile on her face as she turns.... You're worried for her, of course, but you're in no condition to help. She can handle whatever is in the other room, and you can inform Alkin and the others about the noise when they return, which happens soon after. You see Alkin, Vylin, Dusk, and Dawn come out of the forest.
    Dusk already has healing magic in his hands as he crouches down next to you, "Alkin told me you were hurt, but this is worse than I expected. Kin'eer already treated it, I see. Hm, she could've been more gentle. You're not one of her soldiers. Here, keep your arm still."
    That hot-cold feeling of healing washes over your arm, but the usual relief that follows is absent. You see Dusk raise an eyebrow, and then you see Vylin's eyes widen.
    He turns, searching the bodies of the guards, and he returns to Dusk's side as he tries to explain, "L-look! This sword! It's the one you were hit with, right $Player?"
    He then takes the hem of his shirt, and presses against the edge of the blade. It opens up like the tip of a quill, and a bit of blood and clear liquid seeps past the metal.
    Dusk's eyes widen then, and he takes a sharp intake of breath, "Ah, well, that's-.... Okay, give me a moment, you'll be fine, $Player."
    Kin'eer also returns, and she has a strange black liquid covering her clothes and weapons. She's wiping it off herself, but then sees everyone gathered around you and she prioritises this situation over whatever happened to her. She stays silent so that Dusk can work.
    Dusk starts talking to himself, "Okay, simple poison. Locally made, probably new, so typical remedies should work. Dawn, a bit of help?"
    She nods without question, handing over a small pouch as she starts listing off names of plants you've never heard before. Dusk nods and she heads off into the woods again.
    Vylin also goes with her, explaining before she can shirk him, "Hey, I know this cure! If we find trhao weed I can bring it back while you keep looking!"
    She doesn't complain at that explanation, and they both continue into the woods. As Dusk chants magic over you, Kin'eer points at Alkin, motioning for him to follow her into the tower. Alkin does so, leaving you and Dusk alone as he heals you.
    Eventually Dawn and Vylin return, and Dawn gives Dusk the herbs they found. Dusk takes a break in his chanting, and checks the herbs.
    "These are perfect. Vylin, help me administer them while I keep the poison from spreading. $Player is handling it well, but we stopped it in time."
    Vylin nods, "Right. I think I know this remedy. Like this?"
    Vylin starts to mix some of the herbs, crushing them and mixing them in the pouch in specific amounts and orders. Dusk nods as he goes back to chanting.
    It doesn't take too long for Dusk and Vylin to finish dressing your wound, but Dusk looks exhausted now, and your wound isn't quite healed in any impactful way.
    "Sorry $Player, that's all I can do. If I try healing the wound now I might make the poison's cure useless, and right now that's more important than anything else. How are you feeling?"
    |5>[(Link: "-\"Like I've just been stabbed and poisoned.\"")[
    Dusk shrugs, "Probably a good thing. It'd be worse if you felt great, because that would mean that the poison was getting to your head."
    Kin'eer and Alkin then return from the tower, and Alkin looks like he has just seen a ghost.
    Kin'eer speaks up first, "We cleared the next room, and found a split in the path. A monster came out of a secret exit in the wall, and during the fight I opened a trapped door to another room. It exploded but it did more damage to the monster than it did me. If $Player is in a state to walk, we should get going."
    Everyone looks at you, and you get to your feet steadily if not easily. You feel a bit weak, but as long as another fight doesn't start, you'll probably be fine.
    You go to the next room, and in the middle of it you see a slightly humanoid figure laying on the ground. It seems to be some sort of black slime that's melting into a puddle of inky liquid.
    Dusk looks up at Kin'eer, "You fought that thing by yourself?"
    She nods, "It was a clumsy creature that had more constitution than strategy. Anyone with a weapon and half a brain could have taken it, though I wouldn't have called the confrontation easy or simple."
    Everyone mostly takes that at face value, because truth be told Kin'eer has done crazier. Instead you all focus on the two pathways that Kin'eer was talking about. There's a path to the left, which leads to a secret, dark, underground pathway deeper into the tower. Straight ahead there's a doorway with no door, and ash covering the floor. It goes into another room similar to this first one, though the trap that's been set off certainly doesn't inspire confidence.
    (Link: "-Continue down the secret passage")[
    (go-to: "Continue down the secret passage")
    ]
    (link: "-Room 2")[
    (go-to: "Room 2")
    ]
    (hide: ?6)
    (hide: ?7)
    ]]
    |6>[(Link: "-\"Alive, so it could be worse.\"")[
    Dawn actually smiles at that, nodding, "Good way to think about it."
    Kin'eer and Alkin then return from the tower, and Alkin looks like he has just seen a ghost.
    Kin'eer speaks up first, "We cleared the next room, and found a split in the path. A monster came out of a secret exit in the wall, and during the fight I opened a trapped door to another room. It exploded but it did more damage to the monster than it did me. If $Player is in a state to walk, we should get going."
