:: Keep running {"position":"1800,300","size":"100,100"}
	You keep running, following Dusk in front of you. You hear the footsteps of the guards behind you, but they're in full armor so they struggle to keep up. As you keep running you even think you hear one of them yelp in pain, but something else distracts you. You see a river, and suddenly know where you are. You passed this place to get to the wizard's tower, 


:: Leave and find your party [You-hurt] {"position":"1575,625","size":"100,100"}
	Nope. One thousand times, nope. You get up no matter how lightheaded you are, and you walk away. You've walked away from less threatening things, so this brings you absolutely no shame. How else are you supposed to survive adventuring? Surely not curiosity and surely not by ignoring weird sounds, so it's definitely time to leave.
    Finding your party isn't even hard, the clash of steel on steel is plenty loud enough for you to follow, even though the fight is basically over once you get there. You watch the last guard go down to one of Dawn's arrows, and in that same moment your entire party looks at you. None of them seem injured, but you're trailing blood and Dusk looks worried.
    Dusk runs up to you, motioning for you to sit as he gets out his healing supplies and chastises, "You! What are you doing here?! You're injured! Do you know how hard it is to heal a patient determined to put themselves in danger?! Just sit, sit, and give me that arm!"
    You comply, head feeling foggy for some reason but it's going away pretty fast now.
-[[Continue]]


:: Let Alkin go [Potion-get] {"position":"200,800","size":"100,100"}
(set:$Items to $Items - (a: "Potion"))
    Alkin proudly steps past Kin'eer, uncorking the bottle as he says, "You're not the only one who can take a hit and keep fighting, Kin'eer. You need to learn to let people take battles for you more often. Consider it a free favor."
    He laughs at himself as he starts drinking the bottle, the rest of you backing up. He opens the door casually right as the last drop leaves the bottle, and right as the rest of you get far enough away.
    
    ***BOOM!!!***
    
    The door explodes in fire, Alkin flies back. Even though the rest of you were back by the first door, past the hallway, you could still feel and see the flames. They die down fast, but Dusk runs forward fast enough that his sleeve catches fire from one of the paintings on the wall in the hallways, which is also on fire. You and the rest of the party follow soon after, but... Alkin sits up, looking smug and unharmed.
    His voice booms almost as proudly as the explosion, "AHHA! Dwarf beats fire once again!"
    He says it with a huge, bright smile on his face as he gets up. Dusk has put out the fire on his sleeve as well as some of the other fires around the room, automatically knowing that Alkin truly is alright.
    Dusk explains, "I see. The potion wasn't quite a fire resistance potion, but it gave Alkin the temporary ability to not change in temperature. A simple spell that's useful for keeping a room to a desired temperature, but I've never thought about using it on a person. Clever."
    Alkin waves away the explanation, "Yes, yes, but also, as you know, us Dwarfs are quite good at shrugging off fire. Any useful warrior can."
    Everyone just accepts Alkin's pride and moves on. Besides, it's not like he's wrong, dwarfs are known for their fire resistance.
    Kin'eer steps forward, probably trying to cut Alkin off before he brags anymore, "Well then, the next room needs to be cleared. Let us hope that one trap and a group of mercenaries was enough for this wizard."
    Dusk and Dawn both look at each other knowingly. With this party's luck, there's no way that's the end of it.
 -[[Continue->Room 2]]


:: Let Dawn pick the lock {"position":"275,250","size":"100,100"}
	Kin'eer sighs, but doesn't argue. Dawn just nods at you, already preparing her tools. The rest of you step back, just in case she activates the trap, but it's in vain. The door opens quietly, no trap being sprung. Dawn waves you forward, indicating it's safe, so you all continue. The first room is practically empty, basically just a hallway, but you see Dawn's fox ears perk up. You start listening more intently, knowing when Dawn has sensed danger, and that's when you hear it. Everyone stops as they hear voices in the next room.
	"I'm telling you, we're fodder! Did you see how much he paid us?! No man pays a merc that much and intends for them to leave alive!"
    "Oh will you be quiet? We got paid, we do the job. Besides, we got free rein of the bodies and their loot. That's plenty enough of a motive for me."
    Everyone is already moving, you all have done this a thousand times. Dawn quietly opens the door ahead of everyone, and checks to see where everyone is facing. She makes a motion that communicates that they're all facing away from the entrance to the room. Everyone starts edging up to the room, and silently they enter. Dusk, Kin'eer, and Alkin all start going right of the doorway, towards a group of what look like a dozen mercenaries in plate armor, which seem to be the ones deep into an argument. Dawn and Vylin go left to a group of about five of similarly armored mercenaries looting a bookshelf. You're at the back of the group, gathering information as your party prepares for a fight that'll start the second one of the mercenaries notices you.
-[[Follow Dawn and Vylin]]
-[[Follow Dusk, Kin'eer, and Alkin]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Let Dusk Check the Potion [Potion-get Vylin-injured Extra-info] {"position":"925,275","size":"100,100"}
	Alkin takes out the potion, "Ah, right! Nearly forgot!"
    He presents the potion to Dusk, who takes it and starts inspecting it. Dawn also walks over and starts sniffing the potion.
    Dusk starts explaining first, "Oh, it's quite a simple potion. When you drink it, it'll keep you the same temperature for the next ten seconds, no matter your situation. Middle of a fireball or encased in ice, you'll be just fine. I've seen this spell used to keep rooms to the desired temperature, but this applies it to a person. Quite clever, really."
    Dawn nods, agreeing.
    Alkin pockets the potion with a smile, "Well, finders keepers. I'll make sure to use it at a good time."
-[[Continue->Naw, time to keep going]] 


:: Let Dusk go [Potion-get] {"position":"0,900","size":"100,100"}
(set:$Items to $Items - (a: "Potion"))
    Dusk nods, walking up to Alkin and taking the potion, inspecting it even as he walks to the door. He motions for everyone else to get back, which you all do (though Dawn doesn't look happy about it), and then Dusk starts drinking the potion.
    Once everyone is far back enough, and once the potion is empty, Dusk takes a deep breath of courage and opens the door.
    
    ***BOOM!!!***
    
    The door explodes, Dusk goes flying back. Even though the rest of you were back by the first door, past the hallway, you could still feel and see the flames. You all pause, surprised for a moment before you rush forward to check on Dusk. When you make it there, he's already standing, putting residual fires out with his magic. He has a smile on his face as he brushes soot off his clothes.
    He explains, "The potion wasn't quite a fire resistance potion, but it gave me the temporary ability to not change in temperature. A simple spell that's useful for keeping a room to a desired temperature, but I've never thought about using it on a person. Clever."
    Dawn walks up to him, accusatory finger to his chest, her voice a low growl, "You knew the door was going to explode the second you drank that potion, and you knew the counter-spell. You put yourself in unnecessary danger out of curiosity. You gave all of us a *heart attack*!"
    Kin'eer looks surprised when Dawn says this, but Dawn is never wrong when it comes to Dusk.
    Kin'eer sides with Dawn, "If Dawn speaks the truth, then she is correct to scold. She does speak for all of us when describing our fear, I imagine."
    You all nod. You certainly felt a bit worried when he got blown up. It's kinda hard not to be.
    Dusk places his hand at the back of his neck, trying to look casual, but before he can dig himself into a hole, Alkin interrupts, "Look, the door's open and Dusk is safe. We can save the conversation for after, 'cause we've a tower to scale. Right?"
    Everyone pauses, but nods. Alkin is right, this conversation can happen later (hopefully).
-[[Continue->Room 2]]


:: Let Dusk heal you {"position":"1950,550","size":"100,100"}



:: Let Kin'eer break the door {"position":"1800,0","size":"100,100"}
	Dawn rolls her eyes, putting her lockpicking tools away as Kin'eer rolls her shoulders in preparation to break the door. You all back up just in case there is a trap, and then Kin'eer takes down the door.... The door comes right off its hinges, and if there really was a trap then it didn't activate. You all approach Kin'eer, checking to see if she's okay, but she holds up her hand, motioning for you to stop.... Then you hear it too: voices and loud footsteps.
    "Intruders! This way!"
    Ah, it would seem that the tower is guarded by people, not spells. Now you're about to have a fight on your hands, but they're not here quite yet, so maybe there's a way for you to make sure this doesn't go wrong.
-[[Push into the hallway and fight there]]
