:: Let Kin'eer go [Potion-get] {"position":"100,900","size":"100,100"}
(set:$Items to $Items - (a: "Potion"))
    Kin'eer takes the potion from Alkin, who gives it up hesitantly but willingly. She uncorks the bottle, sniffing the contents before waiting for everyone else to get far enough back. She then simply drinks the potion and opens the door.
    
    ***BOOM!!!***
    
    The door explodes in a fireball, and you can feel the heat all the way back at the first door. Dusk runs forward fast enough that his sleeve catches fire from one of the paintings on the wall in the hallways, which is also on fire. You and the rest of the party follow soon after, but... Kin'eer is just standing there, unharmed.
    She looks at all of you, seemingly calm as she says, "It seems the potion protected me successfully." Dusk puts out the fire on his sleeve as well as some of the other fires around the room, automatically knowing that Kin'eer truly is alright.
    Dusk explains, "I see. The potion wasn't quite a fire resistance potion, but it gave Kin'eer the temporary ability to not change in temperature. A simple spell that's useful for keeping a room to a desired temperature, but I've never thought about using it on a person. Clever."
    Kin'eer brushes soot off her armor as she says, "Are wizards not *meant* to be creative with magic? I find this closer to the status-quo than to 'clever'. But no matter. We have a new room to clear, so let us get going. At least we can hope that this will be the last of both traps and mercenaries."
    Dusk and Alkin both look at each other, containing a laugh. With this party's luck you might only have to fight fifty more mercenaries while you disarm ten more traps, and maybe stop a cult or two.
    -[[Continue->Room 2]]


:: Let Vylin go [Potion-get] {"position":"0,800","size":"100,100"}
(set:$Items to $Items - (a: "Potion"))
    Vylin nods to you respectfully, walking up to Alkin, who gives him the potion. Everyone steps back, worried for Vylin but also slightly glad they aren't the one opening the door.... He uncorks the potion, starts drinking, and right when the bottle goes empty he throws the door open.
    
    ***BOOM!!!***
    
    The door explodes in fire, Vylin flies back. Even though the rest of you were back by the first door, past the hallway, you could still feel and see the flames. They die down fast, but Dusk runs forward fast enough that his sleeve catches fire from one of the paintings on the wall in the hallways, which is also on fire. You and the rest of the party follow soon after, but... Vylin sits up, looking surprised but unharmed.
    His voice seems far off when he tries to use it, "Whoa.... That was absolutely terrifying. I am never doing that again."
    He says it with a small, distant smile on his face as he uses Dusk's help to get up. Dusk has put out the fire on his sleeve as well as some of the other fires around the room. Vylin is unsteady, but is very much not on fire when the rest of the party checks on him.
    Dusk explains, "I see. The potion wasn't quite a fire resistance potion, but it gave Vylin the temporary ability to not change in temperature. A simple spell that's useful for keeping a room to a desired temperature, but I've never thought about using it on a person. Clever."
    Vylin nods, "Very, or I'd probably be dead. Is everyone else okay?"
    Everyone nods.
    Kin'eer steps forward, "Well then, the next room needs to be cleared. Let us hope that one trap and a group of mercenaries was enough for this wizard."
    Dusk and Alkin both look at each other, containing a laugh. With this party's luck you might only have to fight fifty more mercenaries while you disarm ten more traps, and maybe stop a cult or two.
 -[[Continue->Room 2]]


:: Let it go. No use getting into an argument. {"position":"2225,500","size":"100,100"}



:: Look for another way [Vylin-injured Potion-get] {"position":"800,275","size":"100,100"}
	You nod towards Alkin, explaining that you believe there's another path through. Kin'eer and Dawn both start scouring the room, looking for anything that might have been less obvious than the book you found.
    Alkin, on the other hand, starts looking over the bodies of the mercenaries. He instantly finds a few items of interest. Some gold, a nice sword that looks like it's made of dwarven metal, and lastly a potion. You tell Alkin that Dusk could probably identify the potion, which is when Dusk and Vylin walk into the room.
    Dusk waves happily, "Hey, Vylin is healed!"
    Vylin chuckles at the dramatic entrance, though he looks tired. His arm is in a makeshift sling and his face is pale, though he's walking fine.
    Dawn walks over, checking over the sling herself. There's no sense of worry on her face, but you have a feeling that she's more concerned than she's pretending to be.
    She looks at Dusk, still with that neutral expression, "Can't you heal him more? It wasn't that deep of a cut, and he can't cast most spells without his dominant hand."
    You notice that her tail, which usually flicks around casually, is impressively still. She's *a lot* more worried than she's pretending to be. Does she suspect something is wrong?
    Dusk confirms your suspicions, "I did all I could. The blade was poisoned and it took everything I had to cure it. But the poison made the wound itself resistant to healing, so I did what I could with the sling and some herbs I had. The poison is gone, though, don't worry."
    He smiles calmly, trying to placate Dawn. It works and you notice a tension leave her body. She must have known about the poison and was worried for Vylin.
    Suddenly, you hear a click from behind you, and everyone looks back at Kin'eer, who has pushed a stone in the wall back with a click. One of the stones was a secret button, and when she steps back the wall falls away. A secret door!
    You all gather around the now-open pathway, and see darkness. Kin'eer raises her hand, which with a simple spell becomes wreathed in blue light, which she uses to guide the way.
    You stop her first, though. Is there still anything you want to do?
-[[Go back and through the trapped door out of curiosity]]
-[[Let Dusk Check the Potion]]
-[[Go back and make sure you really didn't miss anything]]
-[[Naw, time to keep going]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: MAGIC! {"position":"625,525","size":"100,100"}
	You cast a spell that you remember Dusk teaching you a while ago. A simple shield spell, but you try to use it to contain the explosion so it doesn't spread. You have your shield on your back, but that wouldn't protect anyone else, and they're too close to the explosion to be able to shield themselves.
    You see the glint of your magic cover the air in front of you, and not a millisecond later you see the air swell with fire. The strain on the part of your mind that focuses on magic grows, but you've cast spells like this before. It just requires complete concentration.... A flick of flame breaks through the shield, and fear stabs at your mind.
       (if: (random: 1,20) <= 0)[
        The fear breaks your concentration, and the shield breaks with it. You feel the last bit of the explosion fly out of the broken shield, wreathing your face in heat. You feel your shirt catch fire, then, and you fall back onto the floor. Suddenly you see Dusk standing over you, putting out the fire and healing you in the same moment.
        He has a smile on his face as he heals you, "Nice shield spell, but maybe wait for us next time, yeah?"
        You try to smile and nod, though it hurts your face a little. The rest of the party also comes closer to you, making sure you're okay, which you mostly are.    Vylin rolls his eyes, brushing soot off his sleeve as he interrupts, "No, really? I thought that was-"
    Dawn glares and he stops, nodding with slight fear in his eyes, "Yes, trapped. You were saying?"
    Dawn continues, "The door was trapped, *but* I don't see any way that we could have disarmed it. There's a spell here that would've delayed the explosion, but I have no idea what the use of that is."
    Kin'eer nods as if this makes sense, "A true trap. That door isn't the intended exit, therefore there must be a secret exit."
    Dusk wipes his brow, obviously tired from healing both you and the mercenary from earlier. He couldn't heal you fully, but it doesn't really hurt anymore, so you accept the healing you got.
    As he stands, he stretches and points to the wall to his left, casually revealing, "That wall there. The magic in here dissipated when the explosion went off so I can see clearer now. There's a button hidden as a stone, which will reveal the door."
    Alkin walks over to the wall, pressing the stones. After a few tries, his hand presses down on a stone that moves into the wall with a click. The rest of the stones in the wall start to move, then, and a secret passageway is revealed! Dusk claps happily at the success of his insight.
    You go to the entrance of the passage with the rest of your party, checking out the new way you can go.... It's pitch black in there. Kin'eer wreathes her hand in magical blue flame, but even that seems to barely break open the dark. She's about to step forward when you have an idea.
-[[Go to the room past the trapped door]]
-[[Continue down the secret passage]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]
(set: $Youhealth to 12)
    ]
    (else:)[
        You don't let the fear get to you, remembering Dusk's lessons when he taught you the spell. You focus on the spell, making sure it doesn't fail, and the fire becomes contained again. It's a battle between you and the explosion, and in the end you win. You watch as the fire dies inside the shield, and you feel the force against your concentration wane. You slowly, hesitantly, carefully lower the shield. The air inside the shield is hot, but not enough to burn. You take a breath of relief as you feel a pat on your shoulder.
        Dusk is smiling at you, "Good job with that shield. Was that the one I taught you?"
        You can see the pride in his smile, and you're suddenly very, very glad that you learned that spell as well as you did. You nod at Dusk as the rest of your party comes closer to make sure you're okay.
        Vylin seems the most worried, his voice shrill, "Hey, hey, are you okay? Was that an explosion? Did you just shield an explosion?! I-"
        Dawn lightly touches his shoulder, "Vylin. Calm down. Look: $Player is fine."
        Dawn takes her hand off Vylin and he takes a few deep breaths, nodding thankfully at her. Kin'eer takes a look past the trapped door.
        Dusk then points to his left, casually revealing, "That wall there. The magic in here dissipated when the explosion went off so I can see clearer now. There's a button hidden as a stone, which will reveal the door."
    Alkin walks over to the wall, pressing the stones. After a few tries, his hand presses down on a stone that moves into the wall with a click. The rest of the stones in the wall start to move, then, and a secret passageway is revealed! Dusk claps happily at the success of his insight.
    You go to the entrance of the passage with the rest of your party, checking out the new way you can go.... It's pitch black in there. Kin'eer wreathes her hand in magical blue flame, but even that seems to barely break open the dark. She's about to step forward when you have an idea.
