:: Make her go to Dusk for healing [Vylin-injured Dusk-tired] {"position":"925,550","size":"100,100"}
	You shake your head. You refuse to let Dawn continue like this just because she's stubborn. You command Kin'eer and Alkin to keep putting out fires while you make sure Dawn gets healed. Dawn complains again, indignant and stubborn, but you insist again, and she finally, hesitantly agrees.
    You get back to Dusk, who's sitting next to Vylin. Vylin is smiling and talking while Dusk drinks water from his canteen. When he sees Dawn, though, he sighs and puts the canteen away. Vylin then sees Dawn and goes silent. He seems immediately worried and stands to help Dawn to sit. She's hesitant to let him help, because she's just like that, but she does eventually accept. Dusk immediately notices how she favors her left leg, and he takes her left boot off to start healing there.
    You know Dusk well enough to know that this'll be the last bit of healing he does for a while, but you also know that Dawn will be fine under his care.
    You go back to the burning room to find it no longer burning. Alkin and Kin'eer did a good job putting out all the fire, but there's another room to explore, and now it's just you three.... You hesitate, wondering if you should wait for any of the others before continuing.
    Kin'eer tries to convince you otherwise, "Alkin, you, and I can all clear the next room fine, I'm sure of it. 


:: Make. Dawn. Go. [Dawn-angry] {"position":"375,1000","size":"100,100"}

    Dawn walks up to Alkin, anger in her eyes. Alkin, scared for his life, drops the potion and backs up. Dawn catches it in midair, and walks to the door. Before anyone knows what's happening, she drinks the potion and in the middle of the action, she kicks down the door.
    
    ***BOOM!!!***
    
    The door explodes. Dawn's the closest, but the rest of the party is definitely close enough to feel it too. It's hot enough to hurt, and your clothes catch on fire, but the explosion dies down and you pat yourself down, only sustaining mild burns. You look around and everyone else seems to be in a similar boat, though Dawn and Alkin both look completely fine. Alkin is a dwarf, so of course fire has no effect on him, but Dawn? The potion must have worked. For just a moment, you feel like saying "I told you so", but then Dawn throws the empty potion bottle at you. It hits your chest, which hurts, and then it falls to the ground, shattering.
    Dawn glares at you, "Happy now? Anyone else could have done that, but you just have something against me, don't you?"
    You're about to argue back, but Dusk steps between you two, "Hey, calm down you two. We're... mostly okay, and the next room is open. I can heal anyone with burns and then we can keep going."
    .... You both go silent, though are still glaring at each other while Dusk heals everyone's burns. When all are healed, you silently go to the next room.
 -[[Continue->Room 2]]
