:: More information on Alkin [Extra-info] {"position":"100,200","size":"100,100"}
	At first you thought that Alkin was a simple, dwarven, thirty-six year old man. He drinks, gambles, fights, laughs, and acts like any other simple man would. He was even a simple sailor before he became an adventurer, like many other commoners from any port city you've been to. Really, you weren't wrong, though you truly underestimated what being a simple man can mean as an adventurer. He can talk with a woman at a bar like any other man would, and then come back to the party with more information than you could've tortured out of someone. He can walk into a store and buy the most dangerous of potions without the seller even batting an eye at him. He can sail a ship like the best of sailors while still singing the same sea shanty that those who swab the deck would sing. You get the idea.
    Honestly, his weapon and fighting style of choice even represents this ideal of his well. He has a heavy, simple, two-handed hammer he hits people with, and he hits them hard. You could put that weapon into any person's hand and they could swing it with success. But never could they imagine swinging it with as much success as he does, because he has mastered what is simple.
    
    "There's a living to be made or there's Hell to pay when you're sleeping in the cold below." -Keith Power
    
-[[Reminisce on your party]]


:: More information on Dawn [Extra-info] {"position":"0,100","size":"100,100"}
	Dawn is... interesting, to say the least. She's a twenty-one year old, auburn haired Kitsune -- or a fox-girl if you're being demeaning -- and she's just as fierce as you'd expect from a wild animal. She'd probably claw your eyes out if you so much as made a joke comparing her to an animal like that, or tried to do something as simple as touch her shoulder, but that kind of just proves the point. Put simply, she's a jumpy, angry coward, even though she's a coward who knows what she's doing. When it comes to adventuring she's by far the most experienced and skilled, but her people-skills are atrocious and she lacks direction a lot of the time, so of course she'd need a party like yours.
    That doesn't mean it's been easy having her on your team, though. She has a past that gives her a lot of enemies, and her standoffish nature is always starting fights when you don't want them. You recall having to fight an entire mercenary band because one of their members looked at her tail funny, and she took it as a very, very personal insult. It's hard not to understand once you get to know her, though. She has plenty enough scars for you to know that her past has enough demons to explain each and every single one of her outbursts.
    The only details you know come from her adoptive brother, Dusk. According to Dusk they were both orphaned and were adopted under a powerful sorceress named Hecate. Apparently Dawn's family was killed by a powerful necromancer, and Hecate was the one who ended up saving Dawn from the necromancer's lair three years later. That's all he's ever divulged.
    
    "'No' has a death toll. 'Yes' has one, too. There's no correct answer, so do what they want you to do." - August Greenwood
    
-[[Reminisce on your party]]


:: More information on Dusk [Extra-info] {"position":"0,0","size":"100,100"}
	Really, what is there to say about him? He's a young, twenty-one year old adventurer that likes to make people smile. Everything he does seems to be towards that end, even if it's when he's fighting. He refuses to fight if he doesn't have to, and if he can he'll heal anyone who needs it after a fight, friend or foe. That's what you know about him, so it confuses you when people who know him better act timid around him. Usually this happens when he reveals his title, which is something like "Full Moon of Hecate", though you're not quite sure what that is. All you know is that this title makes him an important disciple under a powerful sorceress from the north. That means Dawn is too, but it's no secret how she's intimidating.
    Still, that doesn't change how you act around him. Powerful or not, he has saved your life more than once and has made you smile more than you thought you could as an adventurer. You're not sure about anyone else, but everyone in this party views Dusk the same way. He's almost annoyingly perfect, but as long as he's humble about it you're all more than fine with putting up with that....
    That isn't to say that you wouldn't be curious to see if he could back up any of that inherent intimidation that comes with his title, though.
    
    "Everybody's scared so dance in the dark." -Jamie Lou Stenzel
    
-[[Reminisce on your party]]


:: More information on Kin'eer [Extra-info] {"position":"0,200","size":"100,100"}
	Well, she's a tall, strong, and scary thirty-three year old woman. What else do you need to know about her? That's what you thought at first, because that's all she wants people to think of her. She was a general for the southern elf kingdom of Salendor, so she learned to come across as intimidating. You've gotten to learn more about her, though, and you've started to become suspicious about how well this actually describes her.
    You've caught her looking at little girls playing in the street with a longing in her eyes. You're pretty sure that growing up as a royal elf general didn't quite give her the freedom as a kid that she would have wished for, and as a general she's probably seen more bloodshed than most adventurers do in a lifetime.
    She's also a devotee of Athena, the goddess of war and wisdom. Kin'eer goes out of her way to represent these two things, always thinking about what makes for the best strategy, and what makes for the most efficient way to win a fight. 
    At the end of the day you're just glad she protects you, even if sometimes that's by being the mother of the group that keeps track of your finances (which she calls "simple logistics") or by telling you to get up out of bed in the morning when no sane human should be up in the morning.
    
    "The winner takes it all, the loser has to fall. It's simple and it's plain, why should I complain?" -Björn Ulvaeus
    
-[[Reminisce on your party]]


:: More information on Vylin [Extra-info] {"position":"100,0","size":"100,100"}
	Vylin is a young, twenty-three year old prince. To you, his nobility is honestly so obvious it's funny, but then again, it's been getting less and less obvious the more he's been adventuring with you. He's never been quite as pompous or rude as you'd expect from a noble going on an adventure, though he has been quite naive at times. Not knowing how expensive normal items are, not knowing how to cook, being timid during fights, these are all things that you've seen him confront and overcome, and if they weren't so simple for you then you'd probably find his growth more impressive. Still, you can find some respect for him deep down, even if you have to look for it. It helps that he's a good person who tries to be kind to those around him, even if he doesn't always know how.
    It also helps that in certain situations he's more useful than you could ever expect from him. Anytime that a task calls for pompous charisma, he has you covered. On top of that, he's no idiot and has many random political, mathematical, and scientific facts memorized from his formal education under the crown. On top of that he's been learning magic from Dawn in his free time at camp, and though he can't do much with it yet, he's able to cover his own safety during fights. He has even learned an instrument to help raise money for the party, since his skill with the lyre is trained by a master from his old home.
    
    "I'll darn you back together when you think that you're bereft, and you'll wail, you'll scream, but I'll never stop 'cause it's all that I have left." -Joey Batey and Madeleine Hyland
    
-[[Reminisce on your party]]


:: Naw, time to keep going {"position":"975,700","size":"100,100"}



:: Open door [Vylin-injured] {"position":"575,400","size":"100,100"}
	You simply walk over to the door. You're thinking about Vylin. You know that Dusk is a good healer, but that was a lot of blood. You didn't get the best look, but still, it's hard not to worry.... But maybe you should save the worrying for later, you have a new room to clear right as you open this... door?
-[[Oh no -> BOOM]]


:: Open the next door {"position":"475,400","size":"100,100"}
	You simply walk over to the unlocked door. If the entire tower is this poorly guarded, you have a feeling that you'll get this money pretty easily. Thank goodness, you've been needing the money. You haven't gotten a good night's rest in... you don't even know how long. Inns are expensive. The thoughts of a warm, toasty, cozy, soft bed envelop your thoughts as you casually open the door....
-[[Wait a minute -> BOOM]]


:: Proceed to door {"position":"300,100","size":"100,100"}
	As you draw near, it's obvious how much of a wizard tower this is. There's runes, there's a garden with plants you couldn't name, and Dusk is looking around like he does when he's seeing magical traces no one else can. Of course when you try the door it's locked, but it looks flimsy. You're almost certain that if you bashed into the door you could break it down. Then again, there's a lock you could pick. Dawn is already walking to the door with her lockpicks out, but Dusk stops her.
	He says, "There's too much magic, I can't see if the door is trapped."
   Kin'eer shrugs, stepping forward herself, offering, "If you can't pick it, I'll just break it. I might get hurt but if we push through fast I bet whatever spell is on the door won't activate." Dusk hesitates, not siding with her but also not correcting her. Dawn, on the other hand, glares.
	She says, "If the wizard was smart enough to trap the door, they'd do it well enough that your idea won't work. I've picked trapped doors before, so just let me."
	Alkin and Vylin look at each other, shrugging. Neither of them seem to have anything to add, so, sensing an impasse, Kin'eer and Dawn look at you.
-[[Let Dawn pick the lock]]
-[[Let Kin'eer break the door]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Push into the hallway and fight there [You-hurt] {"position":"1675,125","size":"100,100"}
(set: $Youhealth to 10)
    You push forward, drawing your sword and shield, ready to fight like you always do. You've not run away from simple fights before, so why start now? Alkin and Kin'eer seem to agree, pushing past the entrance and into the hallway. Dusk, Dawn, and Vylin all fall back, though. You think about getting them to join so you don't get split up, but the guards are onto you too fast. There's over a dozen of them and you get surrounded in the hallway instantly, all three of you back-to-back so you don't get flanked. Out of Alkin, Kin'eer, and you, you're definitely the least experienced fighter. It's not your fault -- they've been adventuring years longer than you have -- but you still feel like a definite weak link as three guards lock blades with you. Kin'eer stabs a guard she's fighting as a spear glides across her armor, and you hear Alkin's war hammer crush into someone's bones, but all of you are still losing ground. Some of the guards in the back realize this and start chasing Dawn, Dusk, and Vylin into the woods, which leaves you three better off, but still not in a good place.
    Suddenly, you feel a small cut across the back of your forearm, and your hand feels numb. You've been hit. Some of the guards have started to realize you're the weakest, and they're starting to focus you now that you're injured. Kin'eer and Alkin are still handling their fights fine, and are even doing better now that they have less enemies on them, but you're overwhelmed. You don't know if you can just keep fighting, but you have to, right?
-[[Keep fighting by yourself]]
-[[Fall back and try to get Kin'eer and Alkin's help]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Reminisce on your party [Extra-info] {"position":"100,100","size":"100,100"}
	You think about your party before you decide to tackle the problem of the adventure in front of you.
    Kin'eer is the no-nonsense paladin. She comes from a royal family of elves, having been a general herself before she got into a fight she wasn't meant to win. After that betrayal she left her homeland, and found Alkin and Dawn stealing a boat for their own reasons. They started adventuring together that day, all just surviving together before all of you joined together.
	Alkin is your warrior, though he used to be a sailor. That's unusual for a dwarf but he managed with his ability to solve any problem, though usually through determination rather than skill. That mindset is what led him to start adventuring when he accidentally helped pirates escape the law, making an enemy of the state. He was joined by Dawn and Kin'eer in his early days of adventuring before joining the party.
    Dawn is your ranger, and is probably the most interesting out of the party because she's the most mysterious. She's Dusk's sister, though they're as different as two people can be. She's a Kitsune from the land of Kiveck, though she never talks about why she left or why she joined Alkin and Kin'eer on their adventure. She sticks around and helps in the party, though, so you all put up with her standoffish nature.
    Dusk is the sorcerer, as well as Dawn's brother, though no one would ever guess it. He's just a human, the only one other than you in the group. He's pretty easy-going, though he's easily the best out of all of you at healing, and magic in general, and is also a pretty good fighter.... He's a bit of a main character, and often led the party before you joined, but he's humble and plays nice with everyone, so he's caused no conflict of his own.
    Vylin is your bard, a magician that's great at talking to people and playing music. He even used to be a prince, so he has a lot of powerful connections. Problem is that he has a bounty on his head for his return to his parents after he ran away, so his connections can be hard to exploit. Still, he can carry his own weight in a fight or around camp, even if he does have a tendency to complain.
    And lastly, there's you! You joined the party late, having met them after you got attacked by some monsters at your home. You lost a lot of people and don't have a home to return to, and so you decided to tag along with the party just until you found a place to settle down. Then you found out that you're really, really good at this whole adventuring thing, and you kinda like these friends you've made, so you've stayed.
    Now you have this job, and the tower of the wizard who hired you is in front of you. You've got one place you want to go, and it's up this tower to complete this job so you have enough money to survive comfortably for at least the next few months.
-[[Adventure start]]
-[[More information on Kin'eer]]
-[[More information on Alkin]]
-[[More information on Dawn]]
-[[More information on Dusk]]
-[[More information on Vylin]]


:: Retreat and fight in the woods {"position":"1900,150","size":"100,100"}
	You instantly start backing up outside the tower and into the tree-line. Dawn, Vylin, and Dusk are already behind you, seeming to have thought of the same thing. Kin'eer and Alkin have pushed forward, wanting to take the fight inside. You hesitate, trying to keep Kin'eer and Alkin from getting separated, but it's no use. The guards that were inside have rushed out and surrounded them. You could rush forward and help, but some guards have started chasing you, Dawn, Vylin, and Dusk, so you retreat to follow your original plan. Can't change your mind now, and besides, Kin'eer and Alkin are both great warriors, they'll be fine.
    The woods, though, aren't the easiest to navigate. You're stumbling through with Vylin, Dusk a little ways ahead, but Dawn has practically disappeared. You have a feeling she'll be fine, but that means that Dusk, Vylin, and you will need to figure out how to deal with these guards. You're a smaller group so you're at a disadvantage, but now with the trees it'll be much easier to not get surrounded. This might be the most even the fight gets, but you could also keep running in hopes that you can find somewhere better to fight.
-[[Keep running]]
-[[Turn and fight now]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: Room 2 {"position":"1300,1000","size":"100,100"}



:: SHIELD! {"position":"425,525","size":"100,100"}
	You have a shield on your back, and you use it, getting it in front of you right before the explosion goes off. You fly back, landing hard on your back as heat engulfs you. You try to sit up and Dusk is already there, helping to put out fire and heal you. The rest of the party is there just moments after, some of them covered in soot and burns from the explosion, but none of them seem to be too hurt. You're glad, not being sure how you'd feel if anyone had gotten seriously injured because of a single lapse in judgment, but sometimes that's just how adventuring goes.
    Dusk already has you healed before everyone else gets done putting out fire.
    Dawn inspects the door, which is now ash, explaining, "The door was trapped-"
    Vylin rolls his eyes, brushing soot off his sleeve as he interrupts, "No, really? I thought that was-"
    Dawn glares and he stops, nodding with slight fear in his eyes, "Yes, trapped. You were saying?"
    Dawn continues, "The door was trapped, *but* I don't see any way that we could have disarmed it. There's a spell here that would've delayed the explosion, but I have no idea what the use of that is."
    Kin'eer nods as if this makes sense, "A true trap. That door isn't the intended exit, therefore there must be a secret exit."
    Dusk wipes his brow, obviously tired from healing both you and the mercenary from earlier.
    As he stands, he stretches and points to the wall to his left, casually revealing, "That wall there. The magic in here dissipated when the explosion went off so I can see clearer now. There's a button hidden as a stone, which will reveal the door."
    Alkin walks over to the wall, pressing the stones in the wall. After a few tries, his hand presses down on a stone that moves into the wall with a click. The rest of the stones in the wall start to move, then, and a secret passageway is revealed! Dusk claps happily at the success of his insight.
    You go to the entrance of the passage with the rest of your party, checking out the new way you can go.... It's pitch black in there. Kin'eer wreathes her hand in magical blue flame, but even that seems to barely break open the dark. She's about to step forward when you have an idea.
-[[Go to the room past the trapped door]]
-[[Continue down the secret passage]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: SHIELD(Vylininjured) [Vylin-injured] {"position":"425,625","size":"100,100"}
	You have a shield on your back, and barely manage to get it in front of you when the explosion goes off. You fly across the room and you feel fire engulf you. It hurts, definitely, but the shield mostly protects you.
    You land hard, feeling your clothes on fire and your shield burning hot. You drop it, sit up, and start putting yourself out as your party starts working on getting all the fire in the room under control.
    But then you hear Dusk yell, "DAWN, KIN'EER! COME OVER HERE NOW!"
    You look over and see Vylin lying down in a pool of blood. There's a large piece of wood lodged into his side, and his arm isn't fully healed either. Dawn instantly puts pressure on the wound and Kin'eer inspects the wood. Both Kin'eer and Dawn have cold, serious expressions on their face while Dusk looks like he's trying very hard not to panic. Alkin walks over to you, making sure you're okay, though he isn't really a healer. You tell him you feel fine, but really you're worried about Vylin....
    Alkin helps you to your feet as he tries to console you, "Vylin will be okay. I've seen both Kin'eer and Dusk heal worse wounds than that, and that's when they weren't working together.... Come on, we can go check the next room, since it's hopefully not trapped anymore."
-[[Go check the next room]]
-[[Stay in this room]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]
(set: $Vylinhealth to 1)
(set: $Youhealth to 10)


:: Stay [You-hurt] {"position":"1675,500","size":"100,100"}
	Kin'eer nods, "Yes, good. Now, don't get in trouble for the love of Wisdom."
    She stands, wiping the blood off her hand and turning to Alkin, who also nods at her before they both walk silently into the woods.
    ....
    ....
    It's very quiet, which stings your ears after the sound of clashing metal. On top of that, the stress of waiting for your party is getting to you. You're used to putting trust in your party, but your arm hurts, your ears are ringing, and honestly you're just plain tired, so the worry is gnawing at your heart. That's why when you hear a sound from further into the tower, you're not sure if your anxious mind is just playing tricks on you.
    Then you hear it again. And again. And again. It sounds like a weird shuffling sound, like someone dragging a body.
-[[Ignore the sound]]
-[[Check out the sound]]
-[[Leave and find your party]]
