:: Stay back [You-hurt] {"position":"1425,500","size":"100,100"}
	You stay back and simply let Kin'eer and Alkin take out the last of the guards. Overall this fight was a lot messier than it could have been, but only you're injured so it could be worse. Dusk starts walking over to you and helps you sit. He looks worried for you.
    "You should have stayed still, but at least you're here so I can heal you. Just make sure not to move as I heal you. You know the drill."
-[[Continue]]


:: Stay in this room {"position":"550,1125","size":"100,100"}



:: Swap with Vylin {"position":"775,875","size":"100,100"}



:: Turn and fight now {"position":"2025,275","size":"100,100"}
	Well, no use hesitating. You need to go help Kin'eer and Alkin as soon as possible, too. You turn to fight, and Vylin follows your lead. Dusk keeps running, but when he notices you two stop he also joins the fight. Dawn is still nowhere in sight.
    You turned first, so you're the front line, which has never quite been your job before. Sure, you can hold yourself in a fight, but these are seven trained guards versus just you three. Sure, you use the trees to keep yourself from getting stabbed in the back, but these are no easy duels. You seem to always be fighting two or three guards at a time even as you backpedal. Dusk and Vylin take some guards themselves, but they don't seem to be doing much better. You get distracted worrying about them, and take a sword to the arm. It hurts, but it's your non-dominant hand, so you keep fighting because you have to. You strike down one guard, then another, chipping at them as you use the trees. It's hard, you're hurt, but eventually with the help of Dusk and Vylin's magic you win.
    At that moment, you turn and see Dawn behind you. She's neither hurt nor winded, having not participated in the fight.
    "You all handled that well."
    You can't tell if that was sarcastic or not, but either way you're hurt and you know she could've helped.
-[["Maybe we would've handled it better if you helped."]]
-[[Let it go. No use getting into an argument.]]
-(Link-rerun: "Inventory")[
(alert: (joined: ", ", ...$Items))
]


:: You're silly [Vylin-injured Dusk-tired Potion-get You-hurt] {"position":"375,1200","size":"100,100"}
	Before you even open your mouth, Kin'eer points at you accusingly, "No. You stay down for a minute. You're obviously not in a state to be making decisions."
    She stands, and walks to the new hole in the wall.
    "We have a new room to clear. Dusk, Vylin, stay here with them while they recover. Dawn, Alkin, you're with me."
    She goes into the next room, the trapped one, and too tired to argue you just lay back down onto the ground, resting while Dusk and Vylin keep guard.


:: StoryStylesheet [stylesheet]
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=EB+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&display=swap');

/* ---------- Scene backgrounds ---------- */
tw-story {
  font-family: "EB Garamond", Garamond, Georgia, serif;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  line-height: 1.75;
  color: #ece4d0;
  background-color: #141a2b;
  background-image:
    radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(0,0,0,0) 45%, rgba(0,0,0,0.45) 100%),
    url("assets/dusk.svg");
  background-size: cover, cover;
  background-position: center, center bottom;
  background-attachment: fixed, fixed;
  padding: 4vh 16px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
/* Warmer, campfire-lit scene for the party flashback pages */
tw-story[tags~="Extra-info"]:not([tags~="Vylin-injured"]) {
  background-color: #1d1219;
  background-image:
    radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(0,0,0,0) 45%, rgba(0,0,0,0.45) 100%),
    url("assets/ember.svg");
}

/* ---------- Reading panel ---------- */
tw-passage {
  max-width: 40em;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 2.2em 2.6em 2.4em;
  background: rgba(14, 18, 30, 0.80);
  border: 1px solid rgba(233, 196, 122, 0.22);
  border-radius: 10px;
  box-shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(0,0,0,0.55), inset 0 0 60px rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
  backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
}
tw-story[tags~="Extra-info"]:not([tags~="Vylin-injured"]) tw-passage {
  background: rgba(28, 16, 22, 0.80);
}

/* Paragraph indents come from the tabs/spaces already in the story text */
.para-indent { display: inline-block; width: 2em; }
.para-gap { display: block; height: 0.55em; }

/* ---------- Links & choices ---------- */
tw-link, .enchantor-link, tw-passage tw-enchantment[style*="cursor"] {
  color: #e9c47a;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(233, 196, 122, 0.35);
  transition: color .15s, border-color .15s, text-shadow .15s;
}
tw-link:hover, .enchantor-link:hover {
  color: #ffe1a3;
  border-bottom-color: #ffe1a3;
  text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255, 210, 130, 0.35);
}
.visited { color: #c9a6d8; border-bottom-color: rgba(201,166,216,0.35); }
.visited:hover { color: #e3c8ee; }

/* ---------- Misc ---------- */
tw-passage img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 6px; }
tw-passage strong, tw-passage b { color: #ffcf8a; letter-spacing: .02em; }
tw-passage em, tw-passage i { color: #f3e6c4; }
tw-passage input[type=text], tw-passage input:not([type]) {
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
  color: #ece4d0;
  border: 1px solid rgba(233,196,122,0.45);
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: .2em .5em;
  font: inherit;
}
tw-sidebar tw-icon { color: #e9c47a; opacity: .7; }
tw-sidebar tw-icon:hover { opacity: 1; }

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  tw-story { font-size: 1.1rem; padding: 12px 8px; }
  tw-passage { padding: 1.3em 1.2em; }
  .para-indent { width: 1.3em; }
}


:: StoryScript [script]
/* Turn the tabs/spaces that start each paragraph in the story text into real
   indents (browsers normally collapse them). Only whitespace is replaced;
   the words themselves are never touched. */
(function () {
  function atLineStart(node, root) {
    var n = node;
    while (n && n !== root) {
      var prev = n.previousSibling;
      while (prev && prev.nodeType === 3 && prev.nodeValue === "") prev = prev.previousSibling;
      if (prev) return prev.nodeName === "BR";
      n = n.parentNode;
      if (n && n.nodeName === "TW-TRANSITION-CONTAINER" && n.parentNode && n.parentNode.nodeName === "TW-PASSAGE") return true;
    }
    return true;
  }
  function fix(root) {
    var walker = document.createTreeWalker(root, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT, null);
    var todo = [], t;
    while ((t = walker.nextNode())) {
      if (/^[\t ]+\S/.test(t.nodeValue) && atLineStart(t, root)) todo.push(t);
    }
    todo.forEach(function (t) {
      t.nodeValue = t.nodeValue.replace(/^[\t ]+/, "");
      var ind = document.createElement("span");
      ind.className = "para-indent";
      var gap = document.createElement("span");
      gap.className = "para-gap";
      t.parentNode.insertBefore(gap, t);
      t.parentNode.insertBefore(ind, t);
    });
  }
  var story = document.querySelector("tw-story");
  if (!story) return;
  fix(story);
  new MutationObserver(function () {
    var p = document.querySelector("tw-passage");
    if (p) fix(p);
  }).observe(story, { childList: true, subtree: true });
})();
